ortion of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, San Juan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...Through late Thursday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- The ground remains saturated from recent heavy rainfall over the\npast week. Deep moisture has returned to southwest Colorado, with\na few inches of rainfall possible today through Thursday. In\naddition, multiple rounds of showers and thunderstorms are\nexpected today through Thursday evening producing periods of\nheavy rainfall and potential flash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-25T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Southwest San Juan Mountains; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9312cd85cf27ad49257f3ff9ab7c6f087b55932b.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9312cd85cf27ad49257f3ff9ab7c6f087b55932b.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-23T23:35:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 232335 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 535 PM MDT Wed Sep 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Periods of moderate to heavy rain will impact southern Colorado the next few days with drier conditions across the north and far West. - Widespread rainfall amounts in excess of an inch to over 2 inches in some areas could lead to flooding across the south","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-23T19:13:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...South through southwesterly flow will keep the moisture tap in place as showers and storms continue across the region today. Showers and thunderstorms will develop along the higher terrain along and north of I-70, with frequent lightning and gusty winds expected. The southwest CO valleys an